---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Docs — Godance';
const description =
  'Documentation for the Godance OpenAI-compatible API: authentication, chat completions, ' +
  'image and video generation, webhooks, billing.';

// Endpoint reference — each entry links to its section further down this page.
const endpoints = [
  { id: 'chat-completions', label: 'POST /v1/chat/completions', summary: 'streaming + non-streaming' },
  { id: 'images', label: 'POST /v1/images/generations', summary: 'async: returns a job_id to poll, or pass webhook_url' },
  { id: 'videos', label: 'POST /v1/videos/generations', summary: 'async-only, signed webhook' },
  { id: 'jobs', label: 'GET /v1/jobs/{id}', summary: 'async job status' },
  { id: 'keys', label: 'CRUD /v1/keys', summary: 'API key management' },
  { id: 'billing', label: 'POST /v1/billing/topup', summary: 'credit top-up via Stripe Checkout' },
  { id: 'webhooks', label: 'GET /v1/webhooks/secret', summary: 'signing secret + verification guide' },
];

const chatSnippet = `curl https://api.godance.ai/v1/chat/completions \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GODANCE_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Hello"}],
    "stream": true
  }'`;

const imageSnippet = `curl https://api.godance.ai/v1/images/generations \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GODANCE_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "model": "flux-2-pro",
    "prompt": "a lighthouse at dusk, watercolor",
    "n": 1,
    "webhook_url": "https://example.com/hooks/godance"
  }'`;

const acceptedSnippet = `HTTP/1.1 202 Accepted

{
  "job_id": "6f1c0b9e-2d4a-4c3b-9a57-0e8d4b2f7c11",
  "status": "QUEUED",
  "poll_url": "/v1/jobs/6f1c0b9e-2d4a-4c3b-9a57-0e8d4b2f7c11"
}`;

const verifySnippet = `import hmac, hashlib

def verify(payload, header, secret):
    t = int(header.split(',')[0][2:])
    sigs = [p[3:] for p in header.split(',') if p.startswith('v1=')]
    expected = hmac.new(
        secret.encode(), f"{t}.{payload}".encode(),
        hashlib.sha256
    ).hexdigest()
    return any(hmac.compare_digest(expected, s) for s in sigs)`;
---

<Layout {title} {description} canonicalPath="/docs">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg">Docs</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      Godance is an OpenAI-compatible REST API. If you've shipped against the OpenAI SDK,
      you already know the request shape of every endpoint below, and chat is drop-in: same
      JSON, same streaming format. Image and video generation run as async jobs, and errors
      come back as RFC 7807 problem details; see
      <a href="#openai-compat" class="underline" style="color: var(--color-primary)">OpenAI SDK compatibility</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-fg">Get to first call in three steps</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-3 list-decimal list-inside text-fg-muted">
      <li>
        <a href="https://app.godance.ai/signup" class="underline" style="color: var(--color-primary)">Create an account</a>
        and mint an API key in Settings → API Keys (returned in plaintext once — save it).
      </li>
      <li>Top up with card, ACH, or SEPA (Stripe), or USDT (NOWPayments). Same balance, same API.</li>
      <li>
        Point your OpenAI SDK at
        <code class="code-chip">https://api.godance.ai/v1</code>
        and start switching <code class="code-chip">model</code> values.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-fg">Endpoint reference</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      {endpoints.map(({ id, label, summary }) => (
        <li><a href={`#${id}`} class="underline" style="color: var(--color-primary)">{label}</a> — {summary}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <!-- ===== Chat completions ===== -->
    <h2 id="chat-completions" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">POST /v1/chat/completions</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      OpenAI's chat completions contract. Set <code class="code-chip">"stream": true</code>
      for server-sent events; otherwise the response is a single JSON object.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li><code class="code-chip">model</code> (required) — any text model from the <a href="/models" class="underline" style="color: var(--color-primary)">model catalog</a>.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">messages</code> (required) — array of objects with <code class="code-chip">role</code> and <code class="code-chip">content</code>; <code class="code-chip">content</code> is a plain string.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">max_tokens</code>, <code class="code-chip">temperature</code> — optional.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">stream</code> — optional, defaults to <code class="code-chip">false</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      Non-streaming returns <code class="code-chip">200</code> with a
      <code class="code-chip">chat.completion</code> object
      (<code class="code-chip">choices[].message</code>, <code class="code-chip">finish_reason</code>,
      <code class="code-chip">usage</code>). Streaming returns
      <code class="code-chip">text/event-stream</code>: one
      <code class="code-chip">chat.completion.chunk</code> per event, then
      <code class="code-chip">data: [DONE]</code>. Other OpenAI parameters
      (<code class="code-chip">tools</code>, <code class="code-chip">top_p</code>,
      <code class="code-chip">response_format</code>, …) aren't supported and are ignored.
    </p>
    <pre class="code-block mt-4"><code>{chatSnippet}</code></pre>

    <!-- ===== Images ===== -->
    <h2 id="images" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">POST /v1/images/generations</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      The request shape is OpenAI's. Every image model runs as an async job, so this endpoint
      always answers <code class="code-chip">202 Accepted</code> with a
      <code class="code-chip">job_id</code> — it never returns image data inline. Poll
      <a href="#jobs" class="underline" style="color: var(--color-primary)"><code class="code-chip">GET /v1/jobs/&#123;id&#125;</code></a>
      for the result, or pass <code class="code-chip">webhook_url</code> and receive a
      <a href="#webhooks" class="underline" style="color: var(--color-primary)">signed POST</a>
      when the images are ready.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li><code class="code-chip">model</code>, <code class="code-chip">prompt</code> (required).</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">size</code>, <code class="code-chip">n</code>, <code class="code-chip">style</code>, <code class="code-chip">quality</code> — optional, as in OpenAI's API; <code class="code-chip">n</code> defaults to 1.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">webhook_url</code> — optional Godance extension; where to POST the completion event.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      The full cost (per-image price × <code class="code-chip">n</code>) is reserved from your
      balance when the job is accepted and refunded automatically if generation fails. An
      insufficient balance returns <code class="code-chip">402</code>.
    </p>
    <pre class="code-block mt-4"><code>{imageSnippet}</code></pre>
    <pre class="code-block mt-4"><code>{acceptedSnippet}</code></pre>

    <!-- ===== Videos ===== -->
    <h2 id="videos" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">POST /v1/videos/generations</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Always async — video takes minutes, longer than an HTTP request should wait. The response
      is the same <code class="code-chip">202</code> + <code class="code-chip">job_id</code> body
      as for images; poll the job or pass <code class="code-chip">webhook_url</code>.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li><code class="code-chip">model</code>, <code class="code-chip">prompt</code> (required).</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">size</code> — optional output resolution.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">seconds</code> — optional clip length, defaults to 5.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">n</code> — optional number of clips, defaults to 1.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">webhook_url</code> — optional; where to POST the completion event.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      Cost is the model's per-second rate × <code class="code-chip">seconds</code> ×
      <code class="code-chip">n</code>, reserved up front and refunded if generation fails.
    </p>

    <!-- ===== Jobs ===== -->
    <h2 id="jobs" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">GET /v1/jobs/&#123;id&#125;</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Returns one async job. <code class="code-chip">GET /v1/jobs</code> lists all of your jobs,
      newest first. A job ID that isn't yours returns <code class="code-chip">404</code>.
      Fields are camelCase:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li><code class="code-chip">status</code> — <code class="code-chip">QUEUED</code> → <code class="code-chip">RUNNING</code> → <code class="code-chip">DONE</code> or <code class="code-chip">FAILED</code>.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">outputUrl</code> — set once <code class="code-chip">DONE</code>: a time-limited signed URL to the first output, so copy the file to your own storage. When <code class="code-chip">n</code> &gt; 1, the webhook payload lists every output.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">errorMessage</code> — set when <code class="code-chip">FAILED</code>; the reserved credit is refunded.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">estimatedCostCents</code>, <code class="code-chip">actualCostCents</code> — integer cents.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">id</code>, <code class="code-chip">modality</code>, <code class="code-chip">provider</code>, <code class="code-chip">model</code>, <code class="code-chip">createdAt</code>, <code class="code-chip">startedAt</code>, <code class="code-chip">completedAt</code> — timestamps are ISO 8601.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- ===== API keys ===== -->
    <h2 id="keys" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">CRUD /v1/keys</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Send your key as <code class="code-chip">Authorization: Bearer gd_live_…</code>.
      A key calls the model API only: chat completions, image and video generations,
      jobs and usage. Everything else, these endpoints included, needs a signed-in
      session; a key gets <code class="code-chip">403</code> there.
      Create keys in the dashboard or with these endpoints:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">POST /v1/keys</code> with <code class="code-chip">name</code>
        (required) and optional <code class="code-chip">scopes</code> →
        <code class="code-chip">201</code> with <code class="code-chip">id</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">name</code>, <code class="code-chip">prefix</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">plaintext</code>, <code class="code-chip">createdAt</code>.
        <code class="code-chip">plaintext</code> is the key itself and is returned only this once.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">GET /v1/keys</code> → your keys with
        <code class="code-chip">id</code>, <code class="code-chip">name</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">prefix</code>, <code class="code-chip">scopes</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">active</code>, <code class="code-chip">createdAt</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">lastUsedAt</code>, <code class="code-chip">expiresAt</code>.
        Never includes the key.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">DELETE /v1/keys/&#123;id&#125;</code> → <code class="code-chip">204</code>;
        the key stops working immediately. Unknown IDs return <code class="code-chip">404</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      An unknown, inactive or expired key returns <code class="code-chip">401</code>. A key
      restricted to an IP allowlist returns <code class="code-chip">403</code> from any other
      address.
    </p>

    <!-- ===== Billing ===== -->
    <h2 id="billing" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">POST /v1/billing/topup</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Usage is paid from a prepaid credit balance. A top-up returns a hosted checkout URL;
      the credit lands on your balance once the payment provider confirms the payment.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">POST /v1/billing/topup</code> with
        <code class="code-chip">amountCents</code> and optional
        <code class="code-chip">save_card</code> → <code class="code-chip">201</code> with
        <code class="code-chip">sessionId</code>, <code class="code-chip">checkoutUrl</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">amountCents</code>. Send the user to
        <code class="code-chip">checkoutUrl</code> (Stripe Checkout).
        <code class="code-chip">save_card: true</code> keeps the card on file for auto-recharge.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">POST /v1/billing/nowpayments/topup</code> with
        <code class="code-chip">amountCents</code> → same response; the checkout URL is a
        NOWPayments page for paying in USDT.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">GET</code> / <code class="code-chip">PUT /v1/billing/auto-recharge</code>
        with <code class="code-chip">enabled</code>, <code class="code-chip">threshold_cents</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">topup_cents</code> — top up automatically when the balance falls
        below the threshold. Needs a card saved with <code class="code-chip">save_card</code>
        (<code class="code-chip">409</code> otherwise).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      An amount outside the allowed range returns <code class="code-chip">400</code>; the
      error detail states the range.
    </p>

    <!-- ===== Webhooks ===== -->
    <h2 id="webhooks" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">GET /v1/webhooks/secret</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Image and video jobs submitted with a <code class="code-chip">webhook_url</code> get a
      JSON POST to that URL when they complete. Each account has one signing secret:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">GET /v1/webhooks/secret</code> →
        <code class="code-chip">secret</code> (<code class="code-chip">whsec_…</code>) and
        <code class="code-chip">header</code> (<code class="code-chip">X-Godance-Signature</code>).
        The secret is created on first call.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code class="code-chip">POST /v1/webhooks/secret/rotate</code> → a new secret. For the
        next 24 hours deliveries are signed with both the new and the previous secret.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">The delivery body carries:</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li><code class="code-chip">event</code> — <code class="code-chip">image.generation.completed</code> or <code class="code-chip">video.generation.completed</code>.</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">jobId</code>, <code class="code-chip">costCents</code>, <code class="code-chip">createdAt</code> (Unix seconds).</li>
      <li><code class="code-chip">images</code> or <code class="code-chip">videos</code> — one object per output, each with a time-limited <code class="code-chip">url</code> (images also carry <code class="code-chip">revisedPrompt</code>).</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      Deliveries are sent once, on success, with a 10-second timeout and no retries. A failed
      job sends no webhook — if one doesn't arrive, poll
      <code class="code-chip">GET /v1/jobs/&#123;id&#125;</code>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4 text-fg">Webhook signature verification</h3>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Outbound webhooks carry an <code class="code-chip">X-Godance-Signature</code>
      header in Stripe format: <code class="code-chip">t=&lt;unix&gt;,v1=&lt;hex&gt;[,v1=&lt;hex&gt;...]</code>.
      Each <code class="code-chip">v1</code> is HMAC-SHA256 of
      <code class="code-chip">&lt;t&gt;.&lt;raw body&gt;</code>, so verify against the raw
      request body before parsing it. During the 24-hour grace window after a secret rotation, two
      <code class="code-chip">v1=</code> entries are included — verify against
      your stored secret and accept on ANY match.
    </p>
    <pre class="code-block mt-4"><code set:html={verifySnippet} /></pre>

    <!-- ===== OpenAI SDK compatibility ===== -->
    <h2 id="openai-compat" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold mt-16 mb-4 text-fg">OpenAI SDK compatibility</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Point the OpenAI SDK at <code class="code-chip">https://api.godance.ai/v1</code> and use
      a Godance key as the API key.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Works unchanged:</strong> chat completions, streaming and
        non-streaming, and <code class="code-chip">GET /v1/models</code>. Catalog entries carry an
        extra <code class="code-chip">godance</code> object (modality, list price, platform fee)
        that OpenAI clients ignore.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Same request, different response:</strong> image and video
        generation return <code class="code-chip">202</code> + <code class="code-chip">job_id</code>
        instead of the finished output, so the SDK's typed result won't contain images. Call
        these endpoints with a plain HTTP client (or your SDK's raw-response mode) and read
        <code class="code-chip">job_id</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-fg">Errors:</strong> non-2xx responses use RFC 7807
        <code class="code-chip">application/problem+json</code> bodies
        (<code class="code-chip">title</code>, <code class="code-chip">status</code>,
        <code class="code-chip">detail</code>) rather than OpenAI's error object. Status codes
        keep their usual meaning — <code class="code-chip">400</code> invalid request,
        <code class="code-chip">401</code> bad key, <code class="code-chip">402</code> insufficient
        credit or spending cap reached, <code class="code-chip">404</code> unknown model or job —
        so SDKs still raise their usual status errors.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-fg-subtle">
      Questions?
      <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:hello@godance.ai" class="underline" style="color: var(--color-primary)">Email us</a><!--/email_off-->.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
